@otykier  Thanks a million for the provided snipped and instruction. Super happy to say that even though we were new to Azure Devops, Tabular Editor, and Powershell, we've managed to set up CI/CD solution that allows us to deploy a consistent semantic model to hundreds of clients in a Power BI Premium workspace with a single release. Granted, we're waiting for general release of XMLA write to finish testing, but I feel confident with what we have so far, which is a confirmed model deployment to multiple workspaces with a single release.

To others reading this who may be in the position I was in: the answer to the looping solution was to use Powershell. In short, we use the getGroups REST API call to return an array in Powershell, which we then looped over using foreach. We did some other tasks in this loop, but that's the gist of it. As an aside, we thought we had to learn XMLA (in addition to all of the other new stuff), but turns out we didn't - not yet anyway. Powershell and Tabular Editor is enough to accomplish this dream.

Thanks again.
